[{:db/id "q-102889/selection/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d" :answer/id #uuid "c5ebdd40-eff2-5962-8c47-618659ba7e61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "128" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102889/selection/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" :answer/id #uuid "ade55d68-ad69-5778-be4b-a2b1ebed97ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102889/selection/02ddd28ecf7c540455939ca8b659cf26377dff4fb2cfce0f35f284a540feeaac" :answer/id #uuid "3a766b29-b33e-5bf8-99cc-a9498ac00a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "132" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102889/selection/efc1f4b9a49230e3a3d3e4045f87c921d5c73534634163a59bc9f874eec80485" :answer/id #uuid "62984d86-6720-54f4-83b7-4532c8f1946c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "124" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102889/selection/97308f30e518e82c6f95e608738676bf71c3f2bfc6ba2be7e904645f95acc1d9" :answer/id #uuid "3532685c-1e3b-5f20-9f37-c866ae3ee5c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "119" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102889/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75328b98-6c82-5e9c-bb1c-60fc6ead4211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102889/selection/97308f30e518e82c6f95e608738676bf71c3f2bfc6ba2be7e904645f95acc1d9" :answer-field/choices ["q-102889/selection/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d" "q-102889/selection/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" "q-102889/selection/02ddd28ecf7c540455939ca8b659cf26377dff4fb2cfce0f35f284a540feeaac" "q-102889/selection/efc1f4b9a49230e3a3d3e4045f87c921d5c73534634163a59bc9f874eec80485" "q-102889/selection/97308f30e518e82c6f95e608738676bf71c3f2bfc6ba2be7e904645f95acc1d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102889" :question/id #uuid "a73f708e-ccdf-5d98-9325-8bdc4f82ae5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-102889" :question/problem "How many different codes can be formed by the characters ${y,z,2,4,6}$ besides \"$yz246$\"? Each character can be used only once." :question/worked-solution "The total number of the characters is $5$, so there are $5!$ ways of arranging them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5! & =5\\times 4\\times 3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe code \"$yz246$\" is one of them. By subtracting $1$ from $120,$ we find the number of the different codes that can be formed beside \"$yz246$\".\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}120-1=119\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/requires-calculator true :question/answer-fields ["q-102889/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e49e2595-62a1-595a-8df9-99541bccbdf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102889"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-150014/selection/8d588716b4cd1f8f32dd22b84963b00fbe0174c6e64ffa44aaf9fdf3c1dc4681" :answer/id #uuid "3b84547a-277e-5d9e-92e4-9b6e76ae57ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-150014/selection/fd68b447e7d7722e8db1187dcbf8c29c7aee67d7d98213c2d020aea18b6acb58" :answer/id #uuid "574037b9-99ef-5402-bf32-cbf071bbb2b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-150014/selection/7070b25069d948c4712a183fee9f5f8d8b089e4b7b543a3e2c38e614f239ffbc" :answer/id #uuid "32b003f6-061b-5082-b184-04f5019398ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-150014/selection/a20e462a24b2d65cab7429839bc46b524d25f7f1678fb82590234c6d14c4d796" :answer/id #uuid "f8ba990d-54a8-5b7b-a159-29a3453dab0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-150014/selection/582cd71aeac5eafecb77c6f9f5c1bde2004ee7fc2a9336ab1f49a69e317721e8" :answer/id #uuid "1be6a682-090d-5740-b09a-b04c01b45b58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-150014/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a438b4a-4bcc-550d-b74d-e7ba2c96cf0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-150014/selection/582cd71aeac5eafecb77c6f9f5c1bde2004ee7fc2a9336ab1f49a69e317721e8" :answer-field/choices ["q-150014/selection/8d588716b4cd1f8f32dd22b84963b00fbe0174c6e64ffa44aaf9fdf3c1dc4681" "q-150014/selection/fd68b447e7d7722e8db1187dcbf8c29c7aee67d7d98213c2d020aea18b6acb58" "q-150014/selection/7070b25069d948c4712a183fee9f5f8d8b089e4b7b543a3e2c38e614f239ffbc" "q-150014/selection/a20e462a24b2d65cab7429839bc46b524d25f7f1678fb82590234c6d14c4d796" "q-150014/selection/582cd71aeac5eafecb77c6f9f5c1bde2004ee7fc2a9336ab1f49a69e317721e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-150014" :question/id #uuid "d44ab2d1-b7c8-5c21-9bb5-01b432266f2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-150014" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x+1)$ at the point $(0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,u=3x+1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3x+1}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={\\frac{3}{3x+1}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3(0)+1} \\\\  & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(0,0)$ is $m=3.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =3\\cdot (x-0) \\\\ y & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-150014/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ac7f7e-1e07-57d7-a82a-d6545588c2de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-150014"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325983/field-1/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "5101f0dc-70c0-5b62-a2a9-f4da74e5e623" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325983/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5e7501-56e0-5ddf-8a32-892664f3997c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325983/field-1/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer-field/choices ["q-325983/field-1/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325983" :question/id #uuid "ef999424-e263-53f1-bf60-39690b6d18bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-325983" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/assets/8e6ccf522b5325c3b592ca9470810a95c5491f0b68f000ea774f6555cee0f47f.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a-2b,$ then\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/assets/646b8f1322f815e786f82eb8cfb3fa9e84a3c8d588c94910b0b702b607bfb2d8.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{3}{2}|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-\\frac{3}{2}a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-2b-\\frac{3}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-2b=-\\frac{3}{2}a-2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-325983/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58a49d00-cc58-5228-af38-9369cf31d8c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325983"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-1916/selection/22cc9be582c74452cdb33dacadc3873ee0ce9c17a3a12f1bea855466b3f5899d" :answer/id #uuid "352aa2a8-5555-5333-856a-2a46b33d96aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(2{e}^{x}+x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1916/selection/b3a06429f555004bc732926a5a4d159a51b0031963c56295cf0c6a9081e4f131" :answer/id #uuid "cb6dfc71-ac25-5a81-98df-8ff01479f612" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1916/selection/8b92d3da29a384d91229fc3b06b950e8ac06b7ca650d48205edb034b4e36b9b0" :answer/id #uuid "e887fe31-888e-5b61-af7c-27507a624531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1916/selection/2fc866575c0ea363dbed03e6240fd72e5050876f9dec909e5d70eda48e448b4b" :answer/id #uuid "031214be-a46b-5306-9d5f-e82f68bca114" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+2)x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1916/selection/3529d9b6db59fbefb4cf8ae9bc96ad5b5c8ad67631bf81a2dce691348dd5fd18" :answer/id #uuid "3908dc91-dc16-5891-b6f0-f15fdb9d639e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(x{e}^{x}+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1916/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fec161b-eca2-5ae3-81da-ac4ebf2dedae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-1916/selection/2fc866575c0ea363dbed03e6240fd72e5050876f9dec909e5d70eda48e448b4b" :answer-field/choices ["q-1916/selection/22cc9be582c74452cdb33dacadc3873ee0ce9c17a3a12f1bea855466b3f5899d" "q-1916/selection/b3a06429f555004bc732926a5a4d159a51b0031963c56295cf0c6a9081e4f131" "q-1916/selection/8b92d3da29a384d91229fc3b06b950e8ac06b7ca650d48205edb034b4e36b9b0" "q-1916/selection/2fc866575c0ea363dbed03e6240fd72e5050876f9dec909e5d70eda48e448b4b" "q-1916/selection/3529d9b6db59fbefb4cf8ae9bc96ad5b5c8ad67631bf81a2dce691348dd5fd18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-1916" :question/id #uuid "77390db0-e13a-5db8-9b13-017e21f5f5f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-1916" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2})^{′}{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =(2x)({e}^{x})+({x}^{2})({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2x{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =(x+2)x{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1916/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15a60dd-f6a7-577d-bdbc-148032de94c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1916"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317288/selection/2822695b4b99ce066919355983760e80b763b4de724bf5ace445b49ab3a7be0a" :answer/id #uuid "8e251494-a568-568b-baf1-f74c6dc5609f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/assets/4e70aa30c11b1576699fa384e830d9ad1608963abb0ee98e0cd961d6afb2762c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317288/selection/372fb0212c1591280b463a79822566adee560e27cce8a6fc289534f26c806129" :answer/id #uuid "e0f4c91c-03e4-5256-9490-424d241e0d